          <div class="hero__stat">
            <span class="hero__stat-value">Cotton</span>
            <span class="hero__stat-label">& Modal</span>
          </div>
          <div class="hero__stat">
            <span class="hero__stat-value">Private</span>
            <span class="hero__stat-label">Label</span>
          </div>
          <div class="hero__stat">
            <span class="hero__stat-value">25+</span>
            <span class="hero__stat-label">Years</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero__ctas">
          <a href={whatsappQuoteUrl} class="hero__cta hero__cta--primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Get a Free Quote
          </a>
          <a href="/contact/" class="hero__cta hero__cta--secondary">
            Request Sample
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero__image">
        <img src="/factory.jpg" alt="SDF Clothing loungewear manufacturing facility in Bangladesh" width="600" height="400" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Trust Indicators -->
  <section class="trust">
    <div class="trust__container">
      <div class="trust__items">
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">?</span>
          <span class="trust__text">Lounge Sets</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">?</span>
          <span class="trust__text">Joggers</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">?</span>
          <span class="trust__text">Hoodies</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">?</span>
          <span class="trust__text">Sleepwear</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">?</span>
          <span class="trust__text">300 Piece MOQ</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">?</span>
          <span class="trust__text">Private Label</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 1: What Is Loungewear -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <h2 class="section__title">What Is Loungewear? | The Ultimate Comfort Clothing Category</h2>
      <p class="section__text">
        Loungewear is casual, comfortable clothing specifically designed for relaxing at home. Unlike sleepwear which is intended primarily for sleeping, loungewear bridges the gap between sleepwear and casual wear - comfortable enough for home but presentable enough for quick errands or casual outings. The category has exploded in popularity with the rise of remote work, athleisure trends, and increased focus on comfort. Loungewear includes coordinating lounge sets, joggers, hoodies, sweatshirts, relaxed-fit t-shirts, casual dresses, and comfortable shorts. The defining characteristics are comfort, relaxed fit, soft fabrics, and presentable styling suitable for home wear and casual public settings.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        The loungewear market has evolved significantly from basic sweatpants and t-shirts to sophisticated, fashion-forward designs. Modern loungewear incorporates design elements from activewear, casual wear, and even luxury fashion. Premium loungewear uses high-quality fabrics like modal, bamboo, and organic cotton for superior comfort. Lounge sets - coordinating tops and bottoms - have become particularly popular, offering put-together looks without sacrificing comfort. The category now spans price points from budget-friendly basics to luxury designer pieces. SDF produces loungewear across all quality tiers and price points to match your brand positioning.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Loungewear differs from sleepwear in important ways. While both prioritize comfort, sleepwear is designed specifically for sleeping with lighter fabrics and looser fits. Loungewear is designed for daytime home wear with more substantial fabrics and structured designs that maintain presentability. Our <a href="/sleepwear-manufacturer/">sleepwear manufacturing</a> focuses specifically on nightwear, while our loungewear production creates garments suitable for wearing around the house and casual public settings. Understanding this distinction helps brands position products correctly and meet customer expectations.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 2: Loungewear vs Sleepwear -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <h2 class="section__title">Loungewear vs Sleepwear | Understanding the Difference</h2>
      <p class="section__text">
        While loungewear and sleepwear both prioritize comfort, they serve different purposes and have distinct characteristics. Understanding these differences helps brands design appropriate products and market them correctly to consumers who may not clearly distinguish between the categories.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Purpose and Use</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Sleepwear is specifically designed for sleeping. Features include loose fits for unrestricted movement, lightweight breathable fabrics for temperature regulation during sleep, and minimal fasteners or decorations that could cause discomfort. Sleepwear includes pajamas, nightgowns, sleep shirts, and robes. Loungewear is designed for daytime home wear - relaxing, working from home, casual home activities. Loungewear is more structured, with durable fabrics and presentable styling suitable for being seen. While you can sleep in loungewear, it's not optimized for sleep, and while you can wear sleepwear during the day, it's generally not appropriate for public visibility.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Fabric Characteristics</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Sleepwear fabrics prioritize lightness and breathability - cotton voile, silk, satin, lightweight modal. These fabrics feel luxurious against skin and regulate temperature but may lack durability for daytime wear. Loungewear fabrics prioritize comfort plus durability - heavier cotton jerseys, poly-cotton blends, fleece for warmth, modal blends for softness with structure. Loungewear fabrics withstand repeated washing and daily wear better than delicate sleepwear fabrics. Our <a href="/fabric-sourcing">fabric sourcing service</a> provides both sleepwear and loungewear fabric options appropriate to each category's requirements.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Design and Styling</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Sleepwear design emphasizes simplicity and comfort - minimal seams, loose cuts, gentle necklines, no rough edges or scratchy labels. Styling is often feminine or masculine rather than fashion-forward. Loungewear design balances comfort with presentability - structured cuts, quality construction, fashionable colors and patterns, design details like pockets and drawstrings. Loungewear can be styled for casual public wear, while sleepwear typically cannot. The athleisure influence means loungewear often incorporates sporty elements like ribbed cuffs, drawstring waists, and athletic-inspired cuts.
      </p>

      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
        <table class="comparison" role="table" aria-label="Comparison of loungewear and sleepwear characteristics">
          <caption>Loungewear vs Sleepwear Comparison</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Factor</th>
              <th>Loungewear</th>
              <th>Sleepwear</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Purpose</strong></td>
              <td>Daytime home wear, casual outings</td>
              <td>Sleeping only</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td><strong>Fabric</strong></td>
              <td>Durable, substantial (jersey, fleece, blends)</td>
              <td>Lightweight, breathable (voile, silk, satin)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Fit</strong></td>
              <td>Relaxed but structured</td>
              <td>Loose, flowing</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Public Wear</strong></td>
              <td>Yes, appropriate for casual settings</td>
              <td>No, generally not appropriate</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td><strong>Durability</strong></td>
              <td>High - designed for daily wear</td>
              <td>Moderate - designed for sleep</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Styling</strong></td>
              <td>Fashionable, presentable</td>
              <td>Simple, comfort-focused</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 3: Popular Loungewear Styles -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <h2 class="section__title">Popular Loungewear Styles | What Customers Want</h2>
      <p class="section__text">
        Loungewear encompasses various garment types, each with specific appeal and market positioning. Understanding popular styles helps brands develop product lines that resonate with customers and capture market share in this competitive category.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Lounge Sets</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Lounge sets - coordinating tops and bottoms - are the most popular loungewear category. Matching sweatshirt or hoodie with joggers or lounge pants creates put-together looks without effort. Lounge sets appeal to customers wanting coordinated outfits that look intentional rather than thrown together. Popular fabric combinations include cotton jersey sets for year-round comfort, fleece sets for winter warmth, and modal blends for luxury feel. Lounge sets work well for <a href="/private-label-clothing-manufacturer">private label</a> programs where brands can add their branding to proven popular styles. SDF produces lounge sets in various fabric weights and color combinations.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Joggers</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Joggers are relaxed-fit pants with elastic waistbands and cuffed ankles. Originally athletic wear, joggers have become essential loungewear staples. Features include drawstring waists for adjustability, side pockets for practicality, and comfortable stretch fabrics. Joggers work as standalone pieces or as part of lounge sets. Popular fabric choices include cotton jersey for breathability, poly-cotton for durability, and fleece for warmth. Joggers bridge loungewear and casual wear - appropriate for home but presentable enough for errands. Our <a href="/joggers-manufacturer">jogger manufacturing</a> produces various styles from basic to fashion-forward.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Hoodies and Sweatshirts</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Hoodies and sweatshirts are loungewear essentials. Hoodies offer the added comfort and casual style of a hood, while sweatshirts provide a cleaner look. Both feature relaxed fits, comfortable fabrics, and casual styling appropriate for home wear. Popular styles include pullover hoodies, zip-up hoodies, crewneck sweatshirts, and oversized fits. Fabric choices include cotton fleece for warmth and softness, French terry for lighter weight, and jersey blends for breathability. Hoodies and sweatshirts work as standalone pieces or as tops in lounge sets. Our <a href="/hoodie-manufacturer/">hoodie manufacturing</a> produces various weights and styles.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Relaxed T-Shirts and Tops</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Relaxed-fit t-shirts and casual tops complete loungewear wardrobes. Unlike fitted t-shirts, loungewear tops prioritize comfort with relaxed cuts, soft fabrics, and gentle necklines. Styles include oversized tees, relaxed crewnecks, V-neck tops, and casual button-front shirts. Fabric choices include cotton jersey for natural feel, modal blends for luxury softness, and poly-cotton for durability. These tops pair with joggers, lounge shorts, or can be worn alone for maximum comfort. Our <a href="/t-shirt-manufacturer">t-shirt manufacturing</a> produces relaxed-fit styles specifically for loungewear applications.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Lounge Shorts</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Lounge shorts provide warm-weather loungewear options. Features include elastic waistbands, comfortable inseams, and soft fabrics. Styles range from basic jersey shorts to more structured designs with pockets and details. Lounge shorts are ideal for summer, warmer climates, or customers preferring shorter styles. Popular fabrics include cotton jersey, lightweight poly-cotton, and modal blends. Lounge shorts pair with relaxed t-shirts or casual tops for complete warm-weather loungewear looks. SDF produces lounge shorts in various lengths and fabric options.
      </p>

      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
        <table class="comparison" role="table" aria-label="Popular loungewear styles with characteristics and best fabric choices">
          <caption>Popular Loungewear Styles</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Style</th>
              <th>Key Features</th>
              <th>Best Fabrics</th>
              <th>Season</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Lounge Sets</strong></td>
              <td>Coordinating top and bottom, put-together look</td>
              <td>Cotton jersey, fleece, modal blends</td>
              <td>All-season</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td><strong>Joggers</strong></td>
              <td>Elastic waist, cuffed ankles, pockets</td>
              <td>Cotton jersey, poly-cotton, fleece</td>
              <td>All-season</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Hoodies</strong></td>
              <td>Hood, relaxed fit, warm</td>
              <td>Cotton fleece, French terry</td>
              <td>Fall/Winter</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Sweatshirts</strong></td>
              <td>Crewneck, relaxed fit, warm</td>
              <td>Cotton fleece, French terry</td>
              <td>Fall/Winter</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td><strong>Relaxed Tees</strong></td>
              <td>Oversized, soft fabrics, gentle necklines</td>
              <td>Cotton jersey, modal blends</td>
              <td>All-season</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Lounge Shorts</strong></td>
              <td>Elastic waist, comfortable inseam</td>
              <td>Cotton jersey, lightweight poly-cotton</td>
              <td>Spring/Summer</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 4: Fabric Options -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <h2 class="section__title">Loungewear Fabric Options | Choosing Comfort Materials</h2>
      <p class="section__text">
        Fabric choice significantly impacts loungewear comfort, performance, and perceived quality. Different fabrics offer distinct benefits and appeal to different market segments. Understanding fabric options helps brands select materials aligned with their positioning and customer preferences.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Cotton</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Cotton is the most popular loungewear fabric for its natural feel, breathability, and comfort. Cotton jersey knits offer softness and stretch ideal for relaxed fits. Cotton absorbs moisture, keeping skin dry and comfortable. Natural fiber appeals to customers preferring materials over synthetics. Organic cotton adds sustainability credentials for eco-conscious brands. Cotton requires more care than polyester (wrinkles, shrinks) but the natural feel is worth it for many customers. SDF sources both conventional and organic cotton for loungewear. Our <a href="/cotton-clothing-manufacturer">cotton manufacturing</a> specializes in cotton-based loungewear.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Polyester and Poly-Cotton Blends</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Polyester offers durability, wrinkle resistance, and affordability. Poly-cotton blends (typically 65/35 or 50/50) combine polyester's durability with cotton's comfort for balanced performance. Blends require less care than pure cotton and maintain appearance better over time. For budget-conscious brands or high-durability requirements, poly-cotton is ideal. Polyester fleece provides warmth and softness for winter loungewear. Our <a href="/polyester-clothing-manufacturer">polyester manufacturing</a> offers various polyester and blend options for loungewear applications.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Modal and Rayon</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Modal and rayon are semi-synthetic fibers made from regenerated cellulose (wood pulp). These fabrics offer luxurious softness, excellent drape, and smooth texture. Modal feels softer than cotton and resists pilling better. Rayon offers similar properties with slightly less durability. Modal and rayon appeal to premium loungewear customers seeking luxury feel. These fabrics are more expensive than cotton or polyester but command higher price points. Modal-blend fabrics balance luxury with durability. SDF sources modal and rayon for premium loungewear lines.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Bamboo</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Bamboo fabric is made from bamboo pulp and offers exceptional softness, natural antibacterial properties, and sustainability credentials. Bamboo feels silky-smooth against skin and regulates temperature effectively. The sustainability story appeals to eco-conscious customers. Bamboo is more expensive than cotton but offers premium positioning. Bamboo blends with cotton or polyester add durability while maintaining softness. For brands emphasizing sustainability and luxury, bamboo is an excellent loungewear fabric choice. Our <a href="/sustainability/">sustainability initiatives</a> include bamboo fabric options.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Fleece</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Fleece is a soft, insulating fabric made from polyester fibers. Fleece provides warmth without weight, making it ideal for winter loungewear. The fuzzy surface feels cozy against skin. Fleece is quick-drying and moisture-wicking, adding comfort. Polyester fleece is durable and easy to care for. For hoodies, sweatshirts, and winter lounge pants, fleece is the fabric of choice. Fleece can be made from recycled polyester for environmental benefits. SDF produces fleece loungewear in various weights from lightweight microfleece to heavy polar fleece.
      </p>

      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
