      <div class="faq">
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What is loungewear?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Loungewear is casual, comfortable clothing designed for relaxing at home. Unlike sleepwear which is specifically for sleeping, loungewear is suitable for wearing around the house during the day. Loungewear includes lounge sets, joggers, hoodies, sweatshirts, and relaxed-fit tops. The category has expanded significantly with the rise of remote work and athleisure trends. Loungewear balances comfort with presentability - you're comfortable at home but presentable enough for quick errands or video calls. Modern loungewear incorporates design elements from activewear and casual wear, making it versatile enough for various settings beyond just home use.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What is the difference between loungewear and sleepwear?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Sleepwear is specifically designed for sleeping, typically featuring lighter fabrics like cotton voile, silk, or satin, loose fits for unrestricted movement during sleep, and minimal fasteners for comfort. Sleepwear includes pajamas, nightgowns, and robes. Loungewear is designed for daytime home wear, often with more structured designs, durable fabrics like cotton jersey or poly-cotton blends, and presentable styling. Loungewear includes lounge sets, joggers, hoodies, and casual separates. While some garments overlap (like comfortable robes), loungewear is generally more substantial and designed for visibility, while sleepwear prioritizes sleeping comfort above appearance. Sleepwear is generally not appropriate for public wear, while loungewear often is.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What fabrics are best for loungewear?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Best loungewear fabrics include cotton for breathability and natural feel, polyester for durability and wrinkle resistance, and blends like poly-cotton for balanced performance. Modal and rayon offer luxurious softness and drape for premium positioning. Fleece provides warmth for winter loungewear. Jersey knits offer stretch and comfort. Bamboo fabric offers softness and sustainability credentials for eco-conscious brands. The best fabric depends on your target market and price point - cotton for natural preference, polyester for durability and affordability, modal/rayon for luxury feel, blends for balanced performance. SDF sources all loungewear fabric types from certified suppliers.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What are the most popular loungewear styles?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Popular loungewear styles include matching lounge sets (coordinating tops and bottoms), joggers with elastic waistbands, hoodies and sweatshirts, relaxed-fit t-shirts, casual dresses, and lounge shorts. Lounge sets are particularly popular, offering coordinated looks in comfortable fabrics. Athleisure-inspired pieces like leggings and crop tops bridge loungewear and casual wear. Oversized silhouettes, neutral colors, and minimalist designs are trending. Comfort-focused features like elastic waists, soft fabrics, and relaxed fits are essential across all loungewear styles. Seasonal variations include fleece pieces for winter and lightweight jersey for summer.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Can loungewear be worn outside the home?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Yes, modern loungewear is designed to be presentable enough for quick errands, coffee runs, or casual outings. The athleisure trend has blurred lines between loungewear and casual wear. Many loungewear pieces - joggers, hoodies, relaxed tees - are appropriate for casual public settings. However, traditional sleepwear is generally not appropriate for public wear due to loose fits, lightweight fabrics, and sleep-specific design elements. When designing loungewear for dual home-and-public use, focus on presentable styling, quality fabrics, and neat construction. Avoid overly worn-out looks or sleepwear-specific features. Many brands now market loungewear as 'lifestyle apparel' suitable for various casual settings beyond just home.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What is the minimum order quantity for loungewear?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Most loungewear manufacturers require 500-1,000 pieces per style. However, SDF Clothing offers 300 piece minimums per style for loungewear manufacturing, making us accessible to startup brands and smaller collections. We can produce 300-piece orders across multiple sizes and colors within a style. This flexibility enables new brands to test designs and market response without committing to large quantities. As your brand grows and demand increases, we can scale production to meet higher volume requirements. Our low MOQ loungewear manufacturing is ideal for brands testing the market, launching new categories, or producing seasonal collections with variety.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How do I design a lounge set?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Designing a lounge set involves creating coordinating top and bottom pieces that work together aesthetically. Start with your brand aesthetic and target customer preferences. Choose a comfortable fabric appropriate for your season and market - cotton jersey for year-round, fleece for winter, modal for luxury. Design the top (hoodie, sweatshirt, or relaxed tee) and bottom (joggers, shorts, or lounge pants) with coordinating colors, patterns, or design elements. Consider practical features like elastic waists, pockets, and comfortable necklines. Ensure consistent fabric across both pieces. Create a detailed <a href='/tech-pack-service'>tech pack</a> with specifications for both pieces. Our <a href='/sampling-service'>sampling service</a> can develop prototypes for fit and design verification before bulk production.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Is private label loungewear available?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Yes, SDF Clothing offers private label loungewear manufacturing. Private label means we produce loungewear with your brand labels, tags, and packaging. You can select from our existing proven styles and add your branding, or we can develop custom styles based on your specifications. Private label loungewear is ideal for brands wanting to launch quickly with proven designs without investing in custom development. We handle all production while you focus on branding, marketing, and sales. Our <a href='/private-label-clothing-manufacturer'>private label service</a> includes full customization of labels, hangtags, and packaging to match your brand identity. Private label reduces development time while maintaining brand exclusivity.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
